A||N||1||Manta||Throttle Position Sensor||||1||
Z||000000||Manta||05-26-2000||02:01 PM||||I have been trying to fix my Speedometer, Odometer, & Cruise Control on my 86 1/2 GT.<BR>The car sat for over 1 year before I bought it. At first it wouldn't work at all but now everything will come on for 10 or 20 miles then go out again for 10 or 20 miles. The code I am getting is a 24. Could the Throttle Position Sensor be the cause of this?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||05-26-2000||02:16 PM||||No it is not the TPS. There is a problem with the VSS (Vehicle Speed Sensor), the wiring or the circuitry on the speedometer board itself.  With intermittent operation I would suspect a bad connection somewhere...<P>See the following site for an explanation of the speedometer operation. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/fieroidx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/fieroidx.html</A> <P>(Look under "Articles and Troubleshooting" - "Speedometer Operation Explained". You can also find an explanation of the code 24 under "V6 Trouble Code Guide")<P>Good luck...||||reg||1
